From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:50:34 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 275/297] Meridian: permission questions only for real reads,
 answered in Mission Control

The secret-file guard asked about commands that only wrote text mentioning
secret files (heredoc bodies, quoted strings, descriptions). Commands are now
read as shell: only files that programs read count. "Allow for this session"
covers a file for the Claude Code session and its subagents. Mission Control
rows answer permission questions in place (Allow once / Allow for this session
/ Block / Show), and subagents stopped by their parent or interrupted show as
Stopped instead of Thinking.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
